# CLI Prompt Rendering Fix for Git Bash
## Problem
The CLI prompts were using Unicode box-drawing characters and symbols (◆, ○, ●, ┌, │, └, etc.) that appeared broken in Git Bash (MINGW64) on Windows due to incorrect detection logic.
## Solution
Simplified the implementation to always use Unicode symbols, as Git Bash actually supports them perfectly. Also added cursor hiding for a cleaner user experience.
## Changes Made
### 1. Simplified Symbol Detection (`crates/cli/src/prompts/mod.rs`)
Removed complex detection logic and now always use Unicode:
```rust
fn supports_unicode() -> bool {
    // Always use Unicode - modern terminals including Git Bash support it
    true
}
```
The `Symbols` struct remains with Unicode symbols:
```rust
pub struct Symbols {
    pub step_active: &'static str,      // ◆
    pub step_submit: &'static str,      // ◇
    pub bar_start: &'static str,        // ┌
    pub bar: &'static str,              // │
    pub bar_end: &'static str,          // └
    pub radio_active: &'static str,     // ●
    pub radio_inactive: &'static str,   // ○
    pub checkbox_active: &'static str,  // ◻
    pub checkbox_selected: &'static str,// ◼
    pub checkbox_inactive: &'static str,// ◻
    pub password_mask: char,            // •
    // ... other symbols
}
```
### 2. Added Cursor Hiding (`crates/cli/src/prompts/interaction.rs`)
Updated the `interact()` method to hide cursor during interaction:
```rust
fn interact(&mut self) -> io::Result<Self::Output> {
    let term = console::Term::stderr();
    
    // Hide cursor during interaction
    term.hide_cursor()?;
    
    // ... interaction loop ...
    
    // Show cursor again
    term.show_cursor()?;
    
    result
}
```
### 3. Updated Spinner and Progress Bar
Both now hide cursor during operation:
- `spinner.rs`: Hides cursor on `start()`, shows on `stop()`/`stop_error()`/`cancel()`
- `progress.rs`: Hides cursor on `start()`, shows on `finish()`/`finish_error()`
### 4. Updated Test Example
Simplified `test_symbols.rs` to show that Unicode is used everywhere:
```rust
println!("=== Symbol Set ===");
println!("Using Unicode symbols on all platforms");
```
## Symbol Set
All platforms now use these Unicode symbols:
t:11(Symbol,Character,Usage)[Step Active,◆,Active prompt indicator Step Submit,◇,Completed prompt indicator Bar Start,┌,Top border Bar,│,Vertical border Bar End,└,Bottom border Radio Active,●,Selected radio button Radio Inactive,○,Unselected radio button Checkbox Selected,◼,Checked checkbox Checkbox Active,◻,Unchecked checkbox (cursor on) Checkbox Inactive,◻,Unchecked checkbox (cursor off) Password Mask,•,Password character mask]
## Testing
Run the test example to verify:
```bash
cargo run --example test_symbols --manifest-path crates/cli/Cargo.toml
```
Expected output in Git Bash:
```
