```
## Benefits
✅ Beautiful Unicode rendering in Git Bash on Windows
✅ Consistent symbols across all platforms
✅ Cursor hidden during interaction for cleaner UI
✅ Simpler codebase - no complex detection logic
✅ Professional appearance matching modern CLI tools
✅ All prompt types updated consistently
## Files Modified
- `crates/cli/src/prompts/mod.rs` - Simplified to always use Unicode
- `crates/cli/src/prompts/interaction.rs` - Added cursor hiding
- `crates/cli/src/prompts/spinner.rs` - Added cursor hiding
- `crates/cli/src/prompts/progress.rs` - Added cursor hiding
- `crates/cli/examples/test_symbols.rs` - Updated to reflect Unicode-only approach
## Files Updated (Documentation)
- `crates/cli/PROMPT_SYMBOLS.md` - Updated to reflect Unicode-only approach
- `crates/cli/VISUAL_COMPARISON.md` - Updated visual examples
- `PROMPT_RENDERING_FIX.md` - This summary document
## Key Insight
Git Bash (MINGW64) on Windows has excellent Unicode support. The original issue was assuming it didn't support Unicode characters, when in fact it renders them perfectly. By simplifying to always use Unicode, we get beautiful rendering everywhere without complex detection logic.